ttychatter.mailbot walkthrough
==============================

This walkthrough assumes the enhanced 0.3.1 mailbot is installed as
/home/r94/bin/ttychatter.mailbot and ttychatter.python is installed as
/home/r94/bin/ttychatter.python.

1. Install the program and docs
-------------------------------

    mkdir -p /home/r94/bin
    cp ttychatter.mailbot /home/r94/bin/
    chmod 700 /home/r94/bin/ttychatter.mailbot

    mkdir -p /home/r94/.config/ttychatter/mailbot
    cp ttychatter.mailbot.1 /home/r94/.config/ttychatter/mailbot/ttychatter.mailbot.1

    # If the downloaded artifact is named ttychatter.mailbot.1.updated, rename it:
    # cp ttychatter.mailbot.1.updated /home/r94/.config/ttychatter/mailbot/ttychatter.mailbot.1

2. Confirm the bot can run
--------------------------

    /home/r94/bin/ttychatter.mailbot --version
    /home/r94/bin/ttychatter.mailbot --help
    /home/r94/bin/ttychatter.mailbot --manpage | head

3. Configure IMAP and sending
-----------------------------

Create or edit:

    /home/r94/.config/ttychatter/mailbot/config

Example config:

    IMAP_HOST=localhost
    IMAP_PORT=993
    IMAP_SSL=1
    IMAP_USER=r94
    IMAP_PASSWORD_GPG_FILE=/home/r94/.config/ttychatter/mailbot/imap-password.gpg
    IMAP_MAILBOX=INBOX

    MAIL_FROM=ttychatter@thatiam.vip
    ALLOWED_FROM=r94@thatiam.vip

    SEND_METHOD=sendmail
    SENDMAIL=/usr/sbin/sendmail

    TTYCHATTER_COMMAND=/home/r94/bin/ttychatter.python
    SESSION_DIR=/home/r94/.local/share/ttychatter/openrouter/sessions
    ATTACHMENT_DIR=/home/r94/.local/share/ttychatter/openrouter/attachments
    MODEL_CACHE_FILE=/home/r94/.config/ttychatter/openrouter/models-cache.json

    SUBJECT_PREFIX=tc
    CONFIG_SUBJECT_TOKEN=CONFIG
    MAILBOT_SUBJECT_TOKEN=MAILBOT
    MAILBOT_MANPAGE_FILE=/home/r94/.config/ttychatter/mailbot/ttychatter.mailbot.1

    MAX_BODY_BYTES=50000
    MAX_ATTACHMENT_BYTES=1048576
    PROCESS_ATTACHMENTS=1
    MARK_SEEN=1

    TTYCHATTER_CONTROL_TIMEOUT=180
    SESSION_LIST_HEAD_LINES=3
    SESSION_LIST_TAIL_LINES=3
    SESSION_LIST_MAX_SESSIONS=50
    SESSION_PREVIEW_LINE_CHARS=220
    SESSION_SEARCH_MAX_MATCHES=100
    MAX_COMMAND_OUTPUT_BYTES=200000
    MAX_OUTGOING_ATTACHMENT_BYTES=8388608

Notes:

    - REPLY_METHOD is still accepted as an alias for SEND_METHOD.
    - SENDMAIL_PATH is still accepted as an alias for SENDMAIL.
    - ALLOWED_FROM may contain multiple addresses separated by commas,
      semicolons, or whitespace.
    - Do not leave ALLOWED_FROM=* in production.

4. Store the IMAP password
--------------------------

    export GPG_TTY=$(tty)
    gpgconf --launch gpg-agent
    gpg-connect-agent updatestartuptty /bye
    /home/r94/bin/ttychatter.mailbot --set-imap-password --gpg

For SMTP sending, also run:

    /home/r94/bin/ttychatter.mailbot --set-smtp-password --gpg

If --once later fails with:

    gpg: problem with the agent: Permission denied
    gpg: decryption failed: Bad session key

first test the password file directly as the same user:

    export GPG_TTY=$(tty)
    gpgconf --launch gpg-agent
    gpg-connect-agent updatestartuptty /bye
    gpg --decrypt /home/r94/.config/ttychatter/mailbot/imap-password.gpg >/dev/null

If the agent has cached a bad passphrase, clear it and retry:

    gpgconf --kill gpg-agent

Do not diagnose this by switching to root unless the mailbot service is
actually configured to run as root. Root changes HOME, GNUPGHOME, and the
gpg-agent socket. If a root test changes the error to:

    IMAP error: LOGIN command error: BAD

confirm which config is being read with --config and --doctor. A BAD login
command is usually an empty IMAP_USER, a password containing CR/LF, or a
different user/HOME than the configured mailbot account.

5. Check diagnostics
--------------------

    /home/r94/bin/ttychatter.mailbot --config
    /home/r94/bin/ttychatter.mailbot --doctor

The --config output prints password status only. It does not print password
values.

6. Candidate debugging
----------------------

If a message is unread but not processed:

    /home/r94/bin/ttychatter.mailbot --list-candidates

This prints each unread candidate, its sender, its subject, and why it matches
or is skipped. It uses IMAP BODY.PEEK[] and does not mark messages read.

7. Dry-run a normal mail request
--------------------------------

Send yourself an unread mail with subject:

    tc:{mailbot-test}

Then run:

    /home/r94/bin/ttychatter.mailbot --once --dry-run

Dry-run must not mark the email read, must not record the Message-ID, and must
not send a reply.

8. Real one-shot run
--------------------

After dry-run looks correct:

    /home/r94/bin/ttychatter.mailbot --once

The bot should reply to the allowed sender and mark the processed message seen
when MARK_SEEN=1.

9. List sessions locally
------------------------

    /home/r94/bin/ttychatter.mailbot --sessions

The output lists .log files from SESSION_DIR newest first. Each entry includes
modified time, byte count, line count, and short previews from the head and tail
of the log.

Tune the output with:

    SESSION_LIST_HEAD_LINES=3
    SESSION_LIST_TAIL_LINES=3
    SESSION_LIST_MAX_SESSIONS=50
    SESSION_PREVIEW_LINE_CHARS=220

10. Ask the bot for session previews by email
---------------------------------------------

Send an allowed message with subject:

    tc:{MAILBOT:sessions}

or:

    tc:{MAILBOT}

with body:

    sessions

The reply contains the same session list generated by --sessions.

11. Search or rename sessions by email
--------------------------------------

Search all sessions:

    Subject: tc:{MAILBOT:search gpt-5}

Search one session:

    Subject: tc:{MAILBOT:search-session mailbot-test gpt-5}

Rename one session:

    Subject: tc:{MAILBOT:rename-session old-name new-name}

Dry-run a rename safely:

    /home/r94/bin/ttychatter.mailbot --once --dry-run

12. Refresh the ttychatter model cache by email
-----------------------------------------------

Send an allowed message with subject:

    tc:{MAILBOT:update-models}

The mailbot runs:

    /home/r94/bin/ttychatter.python --update-models

It then attaches the resulting cache as:

    models-cache.json

The bot first looks for a line from ttychatter like:

    updated model cache: /path/to/models-cache.json

If that line is absent, it uses MODEL_CACHE_FILE. The attachment is refused when
it exceeds MAX_OUTGOING_ATTACHMENT_BYTES.

Local test:

    /home/r94/bin/ttychatter.mailbot --update-models --dry-run
    /home/r94/bin/ttychatter.mailbot --update-models

13. Ask the bot for model and router lists by email
---------------------------------------------------

Examples:

    Subject: tc:{MAILBOT:models --all --sort context}
    Subject: tc:{MAILBOT:routers --model-type chat --require-tokens}

Only safe model-list flags are accepted:

    --all
    --sort VALUE
    --modellist-sort-tokens
    --min-input-tokens N
    --min-output-tokens N
    --hide-preview
    --show-preview
    --require-tokens
    --allow-missing-tokens
    --model-type VALUE

14. Fetch the mailbot manpage by email
--------------------------------------

Send an allowed message with subject:

    tc:{MAILBOT:manpage}

Aliases:

    tc:{MAILBOT:manual}
    tc:{MAILBOT:get-manpage}
    tc:{MAILBOT:fetch-manpage}

The reply attaches:

    ttychatter.mailbot.1

The manpage file is found automatically in the mailbot config directory when it
is installed as:

    /home/r94/.config/ttychatter/mailbot/ttychatter.mailbot.1

If the artifact is named ttychatter.mailbot.1.updated, install or copy it under
the canonical name ttychatter.mailbot.1. An arbitrary path or filename can be
used by setting MAILBOT_MANPAGE_FILE in the mailbot config.
TTYCHATTER_MAILBOT_MANPAGE_FILE in the environment overrides the config value.

15. Config by email
-------------------

To request the config:

    Subject: tc:{CONFIG}

The bot replies with ttychatter-mailbot-config.txt attached. Edit that file and
reply with it attached under the same subject. The bot backs up the old config
and replaces it with the attached config.

Dry-run is safe:

    /home/r94/bin/ttychatter.mailbot --once --dry-run

It will not write config and will not mark the config mail read.

16. Other ttychatter utility commands by email
----------------------------------------------

Examples:

    tc:{MAILBOT:ttydoctor}
    tc:{MAILBOT:ttyconfig}
    tc:{MAILBOT:credits}
    tc:{MAILBOT:favorites}
    tc:{MAILBOT:favorite-model openai/gpt-5}
    tc:{MAILBOT:unfavorite-model openai/gpt-5}
    tc:{MAILBOT:test-model openai/gpt-5}
    tc:{MAILBOT:show-memory mailbot-test}
    tc:{MAILBOT:clear-memory mailbot-test}
    tc:{MAILBOT:tty-set DEFAULT_MODEL openai/gpt-5}
    tc:{MAILBOT:tty-unset DEFAULT_MODEL}

Do not send API keys or passwords by email. tty-set refuses OPENROUTER_API_KEY
and API_KEY.

17. Cron
--------

Once everything works:

    */2 * * * * /home/r94/bin/ttychatter.mailbot --once >>/home/r94/.local/share/ttychatter/mailbot.log 2>&1

18. Daemon mode
---------------

Instead of cron:

    /home/r94/bin/ttychatter.mailbot --daemon

Daemon mode polls forever using POLL_INTERVAL.

19. Troubleshooting checklist
-----------------------------

    /home/r94/bin/ttychatter.mailbot --doctor
    /home/r94/bin/ttychatter.mailbot --list-candidates
    /home/r94/bin/ttychatter.mailbot --once --dry-run
    /home/r94/bin/ttychatter.mailbot --sessions

Common causes:

    - Subject does not contain tc:{...}.
    - From address is not in ALLOWED_FROM.
    - Message-ID was already processed.
    - The command is being run as a different Unix user than the configured
      mailbot account. Check HOME and CONFIG_FILE in --doctor output.
    - IMAP_PASSWORD_GPG_FILE cannot be decrypted by the mailbot user. Test with
      gpg --decrypt as that same user.
    - TTYCHATTER_COMMAND points to the wrong path.
    - SESSION_DIR or ATTACHMENT_DIR is not writable.
    - models-cache.json is larger than MAX_OUTGOING_ATTACHMENT_BYTES.
